<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ultraman has the best poses though. The hands on hips one is the best!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says as he does the iconic pose, smiling widely. <span style="color:Pink">He looks adorably silly doing it and you can’t help but laugh, causing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to give a flushed smirk as he asks why you’re laughing and hits you with a pillow when you point out his silly nature. It is a rather wholesome and cute time.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Ask him to pose with his underwear over his bottoms<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> that if he really wants to sell the pose, <span style="color:Pink">he needs to put his underwear on over his clothes, like Ultraman does. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> immediately blushes at this and gives you an indignant look.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ultraman does NOT wear underwear over his suit! They’re trunks and they make him look even more heroic!”</span> You laugh, saying they make him look even more goofy since they look like underwear. <span style="color:Pink">But maybe if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> showed it off, you’d understand.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<if $HangOutNeed.Comfort < 50>>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“N- no way!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> refuses. You raise an eyebrow, didn’t he just say that it wasn’t goofy, but heroic? Why doesn’t he want to be like his hero. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Because mine ARE actually underwear! That’s embarrassing…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s little blush is adorable, so you spend the next few minutes teasing and goading him to try it, but alas he refuses. <span style="color:Pink">When you offer to pick out a pair for him to use, he quickly jumps between you and his dresser, red-faced.</span> <br>
            <br>
            <span style="color:Yellow">You eventually drop the topic, though wonder if you could get him comfortable enough to give it a shot.</span> <br>

            <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
            <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Carter House Carter Bedroom]]
        <<else>>

